# Morse anharmonicity data for air molecules
#
# For use with:  species air.species <sp1 sp2 ...> anharmfile air.anharm
#
# These constants upgrade the THERMODYNAMIC partition functions used by
# the detailed-balance reverse-reaction machinery (calibration constants
# and equilibrium constants) from harmonic-oscillator to first-order
# anharmonic (Morse) vibrational manifolds truncated at the dissociation
# energy.  The collisional vibrational ladder and the microcanonical
# reaction tables remain on the SHO ladder that particles occupy.
#
# format (ground manifold):  ID  N  thetax_1 ... thetax_N  D0
#   N      = number of vibrational modes
#   thetax = omega_e x_e in K (Huber & Herzberg 1979 omega_e x_e [cm^-1]
#            * 1.4387769)
#   D0     = 0-K dissociation energy in K, truncating the ladder; for the
#            neutral molecules these equal the air.tce reaction energies
#
# optional per-electronic-state manifolds:
#   ID  state  K  thetae  thetax  D0K
#   K = 0-based index into the species elecfile ladder; thetae/thetax =
#   state-specific omega_e / omega_e x_e (K); D0K = dissociation energy
#   from that state's minimum (K).  States without such a line use the
#   ground constants with the depth measured from the state origin.
#   (Grouped high-lying manifolds in air.elec do not map to single
#   spectroscopic constants; per-state entries are therefore left to be
#   supplied when a resolved ladder is used.)
#
# ion D0 values are standard-table dissociation energies (N2+ 8.713 eV,
# O2+ 6.663 eV, NO+ 10.85 eV); verify before production ion chemistry.

N2   1  20.61  113062.0
O2   1  17.24   59371.0
NO   1  20.25   75544.0
N2+  1  23.16  101110.0
O2+  1  23.79   77321.0
NO+  1  23.40  125909.0
